  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The entry area has a short explanation of browsing, claims, holding, and collection; visitors may proceed at their own pace after receiving it.\", \"decision\": \"How should arriving visitors learn how the fair works?\", \"goal\": \"Help usable household goods reach interested neighbors while keeping contributions, claims, and final collection understandable.\", \"problem\": \"Neighbors are organizing a one-day fair for clean, usable household goods that people no longer need. Giving and taking are both optional, and no payment or matching contribution is required. Volunteers have intake space, category tables, reserve shelves, a holding area, carts, and simple item records. Contributors choose in advance whether unclaimed goods should be returned during the closing collection period or donated through an arranged pickup.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nA welcome volunteer gives each visitor a brief explanation of browsing and collection while pointing out the relevant areas. The introduction connects the rules to the room and offers an immediate chance to ask a practical question.\nA welcome volunteer gives short introductions to small arriving groups and then offers individual clarification beside the entrance diagram. A common explanation reaches several visitors together while personal questions can be handled after the group moves on.\nVisitors read a simple entrance diagram and take a small guide describing browsing, claims, holding, and collection. The essential instructions remain available as people move through the fair instead of depending on remembering a spoken introduction."
    }
